WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Hey Wes — welcome to your complete start-to-finish walkthrough of Stellar Glass. Every job starts right here on the Dashboard, with your Quick Shortcuts bar and Quick Jump search at the top of every screen.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:26.500
When a customer or general contractor submits a request on your public website, it lands in New Requests — ready to turn into a Customer, a Job, and a site measure on your Google-synced Schedule.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:39.000
Next, inside your Job Files, you can store site photos, contracts, PDF plans, and AutoCAD DXF or DWG drawings — all automatically backed up to Google Drive.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Click CAD and 3D Takeoff on any drawing, and Stellar Glass reads the CAD unit header so your sheet opens immediately at true 1:1 scale, counting window tags right off the elevation.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:04.000
To clean up a busy architectural sheet, click Glazing and Dims in the CAD Layers bar to hide walls and ceiling grids in one click.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Then select Box Width-by-Height and click two opposite corners of any opening to capture width, height, square footage, and perimeter linear feet — or use Perimeter LF to trace storefront runs.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:29.500
Now pick your commercial framing system — like 1-3/4 by 4-1/2 inch center-glazed storefront, curtain wall, or frameless heavy glass — and set the number of bays.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:43.000
Stellar Glass automatically deducts the 1/2 inch rough opening clearance, the jambs, head, sill, and vertical mullions, adds the 3/8 inch glass pocket bite, and gives you the exact glass cut size, 24-foot stock lengths, and sealant tubes.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:02:02.500
Before ordering glass, click 3D Storefront View at the top right to orbit and zoom around the 3D mullions, transoms, and glass lites, preview anodized finishes and Low-E glass tints, and save a PNG snapshot.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:24.000
When you're ready to price or order, click Create Proposal, Order Glass, or Order Framing and Parts. Pick who is sending the proposal so their name and title appear on both the PDF signature and email, and send cut sizes straight to a Trulite order.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Finally, once the customer accepts your proposal, convert it to a Contract in one click, track Change Orders, bill GCs with AIA G702 and G703 progress pay applications, or send an Invoice with online Stripe payment.
